ng health checks after v2.3.1 release - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production release (error rate was 0.18). I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The rollback reports VERIFIED and all three regions now run v2.3.0. v2.3.1 was marked unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Next steps: confirm error rate and health checks recover, and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before any re-release.", "confidence": 0.9, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The rollback reports VERIFIED.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** It is the most recent release marked healthy in production. v2.3.1 is unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc is unhealthy in staging, so neither was a candidate.\n- **Before the rollback:** all three regions were on v2.3.1, with an error rate of 0.18 and the service reporting unhealthy.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the rollback and was paged to the on-call engineer.\n\nI haven't confirmed yet that health checks and error rate have recovered on v2.3.0. The next step is to check the service status, then investigate v2.3.1 before it is released again.", "type": "text"}]}]}